e-secure-channels walkthrough log — 2026-10-10
Worked-case lesson: no command line by design (brief §6).
The "run" is the channel-selection rationale authored and self-reviewed in-session.

Scope: fictional Harborlight Manufacturing (continued): every flow crossing a
  trust boundary or untrusted network.
Artifacts authored:
  - Traffic inventory: 7 classes (customer portal, branch plant link, remote
    engineers, vendor maintenance, admin-to-switch, OT historian feed,
    incident-response chat).
  - Per-flow selection with written rationale + rejected alternative:
    TLS 1.3 terminating at app servers (not LB) + mTLS web->app; IPsec
    site-to-site with traffic selectors, fail closed; remote-access VPN with
    posture check, no split tunnel for engineering; vendor via TLS to jump host
    then SSH (no network adjacency); SSH key-only via bastion for admin;
    mTLS for historian feed; E2E encrypted messaging with verified keys for IR.
  - Termination points named per flow; plaintext segments justified or flagged.
  - Failure modes decided per flow in advance (tunnel down, cert expired,
    concentrator unreachable — open/closed by decision).
  - Operational burden assigned: cert renewal automation + expiry monitoring,
    key rotation, tunnel monitoring — each with owner.
  - Recorded decisions: 0-RTT disabled for state-changing portal endpoints;
    TLS 1.2 retained only for one legacy vendor integration with dated
    deprecation plan + owner.

Self-review checklist (2026-10-10):
  [x] every inter-zone/remote flow inventoried, including forgotten classes
      (historian feed, backups considered)
  [x] TLS termination points explicit; interior plaintext called out
  [x] 0-RTT restricted on replayability grounds (verified RFC 8446 §1/§8)
  [x] VPN types matched to endpoint shapes (SP 800-77 site-to-site,
      SP 800-113 remote-access — both fetched in-session)
  [x] SSH key management tied to authenticator lifecycle (e-auth-systems)
  [x] failure modes decided before failure, not during
  [x] differentiated from e-crypto-applied (selection view, not handshake math)
      and from a-http-depth (when/why, not how)
  [x] no invented statistics; company labeled fictional throughout
Nothing unrun: worked-case lessons have no CLI steps to mark.
